          <h2 class="section-title">Maritime infrastructure spans contested and disconnected environments</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>Vessel and port operational technology systems manage physical processes with national security and economic implications. From cargo handling automation to navigation systems, these OT/ICS environments require platform integrity and remote control at every node — but they operate across vast areas where connectivity is satellite-dependent and frequently degraded.</p>
          <p>MEAICON designs maritime infrastructure that addresses these dual challenges: OT security for vessel and port environments, and resilient edge computing that operates grid-independent for weeks without resupply. Post-quantum-ready cryptography protects long-term data confidentiality, while geo-fencing enforces compliance with regulated maritime zones.</p>
